  of asserting that a value matches a specific pattern, it asserts that a boolean
  value evaluates to <code>True</code>.
</p>
<p>
  Like the other panicking keywords, the <code>as</code> keyword can be used to
  add a custom message to an assertion. This will be shown instead of the generic
  \"Assertion failed\" message if the value evaluates to <code>False</code>.
</p>
<p>
  Bool <code>assert</code> is designed to be used in test code, and should almost
  never be used in applications or libraries.
</p>",
    code: "pub fn main() {
  assert add(1, 2) == 3

  assert add(1, 2) < add(1, 3)

